# --- Protobuf Generated Files (Internal) ---
# Note: Keep generated code in repo if specifically required for build consistency,
# but usually internal/proto/*.pb.go should be ignored if generated on-the-fly.
# We follow a "check-in generated code" policy for GAPI/Goblin currently,
# so we only ignore intermediate buf artifacts.
buf.lock
buf.gen.yaml.lock
.bufbuild/

# --- Python Cache and build artifacts ---
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
venv/
dist/

# --- gopy-generated Python bindings (GAPI-DIV-029) ---
# Deliberate exception to the "check-in generated code" policy noted
# above. gopy emits these in a different order on every run (it iterates
# a map), so a no-op regeneration rewrote the exported-function blocks
# in a fresh permutation and dirtied every working tree. Proven a pure
# permutation: sorting the lines of two successive runs yields identical
# checksums. The compiled half (*.so) was already ignored, and one of
# these files embeds a CPython ABI and architecture in its name, so it
# could never have been correct for another host anyway.
#
# These are regenerated by 'mage python:build', which runs in the dev
# shell and in both CI jobs. Nothing here is hand-written; do not
# re-add these to version control.
adk/python/gapi/native/adk.c
adk/python/gapi/native/adk.go
adk/python/gapi/native/adk.py
adk/python/gapi/native/adk_go.h
adk/python/gapi/native/build.py
adk/python/gapi/native/go.py
adk/python/gapi/native/__init__.py
adk/python/gapi/native/_adk.*.h

# --- Nix Build Outputs ---
# No trailing slash: 'nix build' creates result as a SYMLINK to the
# store path, and a trailing slash matches only directories, so
# 'result/' ignored nothing that nix actually produces.
result
result-*

